train/train_dreambooth_lora_qwenimage21_img2img.py is a copy of

  https://github.com/huggingface/diffusers
  path:   examples/dreambooth/train_dreambooth_lora_qwenimage21_img2img.py
  commit: e0abab83b5df05de9e7abd788643c1a7c1e42e28

Copyright 2025 The HuggingFace Inc. team. Licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. The upstream license header is kept verbatim at the top of the file
(the upstream header itself ends at "...governing permissions and"; it was not
edited here).

Modifications (the only changes to the upstream file; full diff in
train/hooks.patch, 4 call sites, no change to the training logic):

  1. After the prompt-embedding cache is filled, and before the text encoder
     and VAE are freed: `train_hooks.prepare(...)` encodes a fixed held-out test
     set (prompt embeddings, target / condition latents, fixed noise).
  2. Before the training loop: `train_hooks.on_step(0, ...)` evaluates the base
     model (the LoRA B matrices start at zero).
  3. After every optimizer step: `train_hooks.log_train_step(...)` appends loss,
     lr and the sampled sigma to train.jsonl.
  4. After every optimizer step: `train_hooks.on_step(step, ...)` runs the
     periodic held-out probe loss, validation sampling, and LoRA snapshot.

The hooks live in train/train_hooks.py (original code of this project). They only
read the model in eval mode under torch.no_grad and write logs / images / LoRA files.

